{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ParseStrategy","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Decodable","preciseIdentifier":"s:Se","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encodable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SE","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy"},{"text":" allows you to convert a formatted representation into a data type, using one of two approaches:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Initialize the data type by calling an initializer of that type that takes a formatted instance and a parse strategy as parameters. For example, you can create a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Decimal","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" from a formatted string with the initializer "},{"code":"Decimal\/init(_:format:lenient:)-6fk71","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a parse strategy and call its "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy\/parse(_:)"},{"text":" method on one or more formatted instances.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy"},{"text":" is closely related to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle"},{"text":", which provides the opposite conversion: from data type to formatted representation. To use a parse strategy, you create a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle"},{"text":" to define the representation you expect, then access the style’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parseStrategy"},{"text":" property to get a strategy instance.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example creates a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Decimal\/FormatStyle\/Currency"},{"text":" format style that uses US dollars and US English number-formatting conventions. It then creates a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Decimal"},{"text":" instance by providing a formatted string to parse and the format style’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Decimal\/FormatStyle\/Currency\/parseStrategy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let style = Decimal.FormatStyle.Currency(code: \"USD\",","locale: Locale(identifier: \"en_US\"))","let parsed = try? Decimal(\"$12,345.67\",","strategy: style.parseStrategy) \/\/ 12345.67"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Protocol","symbolKind":"protocol","modules":[{"name":"FoundationEssentials"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ParseStrategy","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ParseStrategy","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:20FoundationEssentials13ParseStrategyP","platforms":[{"name":"iOS","beta":false,"unavaila